  "notes": "Savola Group Company (ticker 2050) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/385_0_2026-03-09...). Auditor: Deloitte and Touche & Co. (Chartered Accountants); auditor's report Jeddah, 19 Ramadan 1447H / 8 March 2026 (used as filed_at - the filed PDF carries no separate board-approval date note). Amounts are presented in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). The five primary statements (printed FS pages 7-14) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.4x); the notes are digital text. Consolidated group with non-controlling interests. IFRS 5: Savola has discontinued operations in both years (FY2025 loss SAR 7,585 thousand; FY2024 loss SAR 1,440,202 thousand - the Panda / retail and other disposals). The reported 'Profit before zakat and income tax' (SAR 861,708 thousand FY2025) is a continuing-operations figure, so income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is NOT carried; continuing_operations_income (948,084) and discontinued_operations_income (-7,585) are carried and net_income = continuing + discontinued is checked. FY2024's continuing result also included a one-off SAR 11,554,662 thousand 'Gain on distribution of investment in equity-accounted investee' (the in-kind distribution of the Almarai stake) and a SAR 139,001 thousand 'Loss on derecognition of investment in equity-accounted investee' - carried together as other_nonoperating_income for FY2024. income_taxes_and_zakat sums the reported 'Income tax expense' and 'Zakat reversal / (expense), net' - a net SAR 86,376 thousand credit in FY2025 (a large prior-year zakat reversal) and a net SAR 581,125 thousand charge in FY2024. operating_income is the reported 'Results from operating activities'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Share of results in equity-accounted investees, net of zakat and tax'; impairment_charges combines 'Impairment charge, net' and 'Net impairment (loss)/reversal on financial assets'; other_income is 'Other operating income, net'. investment_property_value is 'Investment property'; long_term_investments is the non-current 'Investments' line; short_term_investments is the current 'Investments' line. additional_paid_in_capital is 'Share premium'; treasury_shares is 'Shares held under employees' share based payment plan'; other_reserves combines the 'General reserve', 'Other reserves', 'Effect of transactions with non-controlling interests without change in control' and the 'Foreign currency translation reserve'. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current 'Loans and borrowings' (nil non-current at FY2025); lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the non-current / current lease liabilities. defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employee benefits liabilities'; provisions is 'Provision against asset restoration'; accrued_expenses is 'Accrued and other liabilities'; contract_liabilities is 'Contract liabilities'; other_current_liabilities is the FY2024 'Put liability' (nil at FY2025); zakat_payable sums 'Accrued income tax' and 'Accrued zakat'. depreciation_amortization is the 'Depreciation and amortisation' add-back on the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Acquisition of property, plant and equipment'; interest_paid sums 'Finance cost paid on loans and borrowings' and 'Finance cost paid on lease liabilities'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid to the owners of the Company' (a separate SAR 72,492 / 53,016 thousand went to non-controlling interests). foreign_exchange_effect is the 'Effect of movement in exchange rates on cash and cash equivalents'. The cash-flow closing balance (SAR 842,697 thousand) is below the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line (SAR 904,137 thousand) because the cash-flow 'cash and cash equivalents' is net of bank overdrafts, so the cash-to-balance-sheet cross-check warns (expected). Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 7-8, profit or loss and OCI 9-10, changes in equity 11-12, cash flows 13-14.",
